    "title": "Austin Cracks Top 6 for Women in Tech, but a 20 Percent Pay Gap Still Lingers - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sophie Leclerc ,\n12 hours ago Austin has climbed into the top 10 nationally for women working in tech, landing at No. 6 among the 50 biggest U.S. cities in a new study measuring where female tech workers earn the most relative to their male peers and make up the largest share of the industry. More than 12,000 women now work in tech roles across the city, representing nearly 23 percent of Austin's total tech workforce, even though tech workers overall make up less than 9 percent of the city's total workforce. Read full article",
